      </h2>

      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #cbd5e1;">
          <h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">
            What essential columns should a wedding RSVP tracking spreadsheet contain?
          </h4>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.6;">
            A complete RSVP tracking sheet must track: Household Name, Individual Guest Name, RSVP Status (Accepted/Declined/Pending), Entree Choice (Beef/Chicken/Fish/Vegan), Specific Medical Allergies (e.g., Celiac, Anaphylactic Peanut), Plus-One Full Legal Name, Table Number, and Lodging/Hotel Block confirmation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #cbd5e1;">
          <h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">
            Is an online wedding RSVP better than paper response cards?
          </h4>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.6;">
            Online RSVPs via QR codes or custom forms reduce RSVP friction by 65%, save couples $180-$350 in return postage and printing, eliminate lost mail delays, and automatically enforce plus-one limits so uninvited guests cannot write in extra attendees.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #cbd5e1;">
          <h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">
            How should couples organize dietary restrictions for their caterer?
          </h4>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.6;">
            Submit a dedicated 'Dietary Exception Manifest' to the catering chef 14 days before the wedding that cross-references guest name, exact table number, seat position, and medical allergy severity to prevent cross-contamination in banquet kitchens.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #cbd5e1;">
          <h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">
            What percentage of wedding guests fail to RSVP by the deadline?
          </h4>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.6;">
            Between 20% and 35% of invited guests miss the initial RSVP deadline. Implementing a structured 3-phase follow-up cadence (Day +2 text, Day +5 phone call, Day +8 final cutoff notice) recovers 95% of missing responses within one week.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #cbd5e1;">
          <h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">
            How do you handle uninvited plus-ones written on RSVP cards?
          </h4>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.6;">
